@startuml
title ProofSieve · How to use the application
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #15283F
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #526B8A
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #8CA6C9
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #EDF4FC
skinparam nodesep 27
skinparam ranksep 34

rectangle "**ProofSieve**\nWhat do you want to do?" as Start #DFECFC

together {
    rectangle "**01  Configure a rule**\nAdmin · Guard\nChoose a /verify path, edit and test\nan ODRL or SHACL draft, then save" as Author
    rectangle "**02  Test an input**\nVerifier · Builder and Guard\nPrepare or load data, choose a compatible\nendpoint and run the check" as Test
    rectangle "**03  Integrate a service**\nClient · Swagger and API\nDiscover allowed paths and call\na saved /verify endpoint" as Integrate
    rectangle "**Explore worked examples**\nVerification Lab\nTry synthetic cases and export\nthe edited example" as Lab #F4F5F7
}

rectangle "**Saved endpoint**\nChecks the input and applies the configured rule" as Check #DFECFC
rectangle "**04  Deliver an approved request**\nForwarding-enabled decision endpoints\nSend the original body to a fixed HTTPS receiver\nand report the delivery state" as Forward #E3F4EC
rectangle "**Return the configured result**\nBoolean, Guard status, URL in JSON\nor recorded decision with any delivery state" as Respond

Start -down-> Author
Start -down-> Test
Start -down-> Integrate
Start -down-> Lab
Author -[dashed]down-> Check : saved rule
Test -down-> Check
Integrate -down-> Check
Check -down-> Forward : approval + forwarding configured
Check -down-> Respond : other outcomes
Forward -down-> Respond
@enduml
